    "restart": "Clean scheduler/store reopen only after local owners are empty and no surviving listening has an aborted request; late external requests may still belong to deleted listenings. Does not model SIGKILL or recovery/retry of surviving cancelled knowledge jobs.",
    "duplicate": "Repeated resolve/reject of one JS Promise is a business stutter. onUsage is a distinct real repeated callback and upserts only the original relation request journal row.",
    "aborted": "Logical request invalidation before its business continuation. Not a direct copy of knowledge child scope signal.aborted after successful scope cleanup.",
    "usage": "Normalized presence/nonlate-or-late attribution for the original relation_requests(job_id,attempt), not the exact durable outcome string: commit may change response_received to complete/partial, and another real onUsage can overwrite it. No knowledge usage journal is invented."
